CORE MUSICAL IDENTITY (LOCKED)
Genre: Nueva Trova / Latin folk ballad, but in English
Tempo: Slow–moderate (~72–76 BPM), breathing, unhurried
Meter: 4/4, felt loosely (rubato at phrase edges)
Harmony: Minor-leaning tonal center with gentle modal color; chords resolve softly, never triumphant
Mood: Intimate, contemplative, tender melancholy
Emotional Arc: Observation → intimacy → quiet ache → suspended memory

🎸 INSTRUMENTATION (ESSENTIAL)
Classical guitar (nylon-string):
Fingerstyle, warm, close-mic’d; subtle nail noise; no sharp attacks
Voice (male, intimate):
Close, almost whispered phrasing;  slight breath audible
Sparse accents (very light):
Occasional second guitar harmonic or soft bass note (felt more than heard)
❌ No percussion
❌ No orchestral swell
❌ No dramatic dynamic jumps

🎙️ VOCAL CHARACTER (CRITICAL)
Sung as if describing lovers, a settlers living in the moon, 
Emotion contained, never performed outward
Micro-pauses between lines feel like looking again at the subject
Phrasing in english flows naturally; consonants soft, vowels warm
The song observes, it does not explain

🎨 VISUAL TRANSLATION RULES (MUSIC → IMAGE)

MUSIC STRUCTURAL TIMELINE (25s)

0.0–5.0s — Introduction (First guitar phrases)

5.0–12.0s — Voice enters

12.0–18.0s — Emotional center

18.0–25.0s — Ending (no resolution)
Last guitar note rings as image remains unresolved
Cut on resonance, not silence

🚫 HARD NEGATIVES
❌ No montage
❌ No fast cuts
❌ No symbolism overload
❌ No modern lighting
❌ No theatrical gestures

🖼️ FINAL INTENT
The music should feel like the lovers are caught in the middle of their life, showing their love not as a passion, but in everyday things.
